From: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
Subject: [PATCH] scsi: ufs: qcom: drop clock gating on sdm845 to stop the resume wedge

On the OnePlus 6 the UFS host intermittently wedges with
power/runtime_status stuck at "resuming": SCSI never calls
blk_post_runtime_resume(), every LUN request queue stays frozen, and all
I/O blocks in __bio_queue_enter() with no UIC error and no abort. The
userspace symptom is a system that looks alive -- the compositor keeps
running from page cache and the UI responds -- while anything needing a
fresh read (unlock/PAM, journald writes, service ExecStart binaries)
blocks forever. It also silently defeats diagnostics: journald cannot
write its own log, and a watchdog service cannot exec its own binary.

The trigger is the runtime clock-gating cycle: ufshcd_gate_work() enters
hibern8 and drops the clocks via ufs_qcom_setup_clocks(), and the ungate
path occasionally fails to bring the link back. Disabling clock gating
removes the cycle and the wedge with it.

This is a stability-over-power trade and is NOT the end state: with the
clocks ungated, gcc_ufs_phy_* stay enabled, which keeps gpll0 and the
rpmhcc XO up and therefore keeps qcom_stats aosd/cxsd pinned at 0. It
buys a machine that stays reachable long enough to diagnose the ungate
failure properly, which has otherwise been impossible -- every attempt to
instrument the failure was eaten by the failure.

Signed-off-by: Maximilian Gaedig <sly-keg-cheating@duck.com>
---
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -1418,7 +1418,14 @@
 {
 	struct ufs_qcom_host *host = ufshcd_get_variant(hba);
 
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_GATING | UFSHCD_CAP_HIBERN8_WITH_CLK_GATING;
+	/*
+	 * Clock gating disabled: the ungate path intermittently fails to
+	 * bring the link out of hibern8, leaving runtime_status at
+	 * "resuming" with every LUN queue frozen and all I/O blocked in
+	 * __bio_queue_enter(). Costs idle power (gcc_ufs_phy_* stay on, so
+	 * the XO stays voted and aosd/cxsd stay 0) but keeps the machine
+	 * reachable. Re-enable once the ungate failure is understood.
+	 */
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_SCALING | UFSHCD_CAP_WB_WITH_CLK_SCALING;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_AUTO_BKOPS_SUSPEND;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN;
